    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37777" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐοικότως</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰκότως</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκότως</span></b> , Adv. of
			part.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐοικώς,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>similarly, like,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					915
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>reasonably, fairly, naturally, as was to be expected,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				403
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ εἰ.</span>
				un<i>fairly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.37
			</span></i>; freq. emphat. at the close of a sentence or clause,
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				77
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				2.93
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				1.48
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
